questions.question:
A page changes its layout on small screens.
```html
<head>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
</head>
<body>
  <h1 class="title">My Blog</h1>
  <nav class="menu">Home | Posts | About</nav>
</body>
```
```css
.title { font-size: 32px; }
.menu { display: block; }
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .title { font-size: 20px; }
  .menu { display: none; }
}
```
(a) The page is viewed on a laptop with a screen 1000px wide. What size is the title, and is the menu shown? Explain why.
(b) The page is viewed on a phone with a screen 400px wide. What size is the title, and is the menu shown? Explain why.
(c) What is the purpose of the `<meta name="viewport">` tag in the head?

Given `<p class="note" id="intro">Hi</p>` and the CSS:
```css
p { color: blue; }
.note { color: green; }
#intro { color: red; }
```
(a) What colour is the paragraph? Explain using specificity.
(b) If the `#intro` rule is removed, which rule wins and why?
(c) Why is `!important` generally discouraged?

```css
.card {
  width: 300px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 5px solid black;
  box-sizing: content-box;
}
```
(a) What is the total horizontal space the `.card` takes up?
(b) How does adding `box-sizing: border-box` change this?
(c) When would you prefer `rem` over `px` for a font size?

```css
.row {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
}
```
(a) What does `justify-content` control, and how is that different from `align-items`?
(b) How would you change the CSS so the children stack vertically and are centred?
(c) What does `flex: 1` on a child do?

```css
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
  gap: 16px;
}
```
(a) How many columns are created, and how does `1fr 2fr` split the width?
(b) What is `gap` for?
(c) Why do many teams reach for a CSS framework or utility classes instead of writing every rule by hand?

```css
.card { position: relative; }
.badge {
  position: absolute;
  top: 8px;
  right: 8px;
  z-index: 10;
}
```
(a) Relative to what is `.badge` positioned, and why does `.card` need `position: relative`?
(b) What does `z-index` control, and why does it sometimes appear to have no effect?
(c) What is the difference between `position: relative` and `position: absolute`?

一个商品卡片放在 320px 的侧栏列里，CSS 如下：
```css
.card {
  box-sizing: content-box;
  width: 300px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 3px solid #333;
}
.card + .card { margin-top: 32px; } /* 上一张卡片有 margin-bottom: 16px */
```
(a) 这张卡片真实占用的总宽度是多少？为什么 content-box 会得出这个数？(b) 卡片为什么会溢出 320px 的列？加上 `box-sizing: border-box` 后数字怎么变？(c) 设计者以为两张卡片间距是 16 + 32 = 48px，实际却只有 32px，为什么？如何得到确定的 48px？

